                        "review": "Heliborne is the rare helicopter game that remembers missiles do not capture territory.\r\n\r\nAttack helicopters erase armour. Scouts find targets. Transports land under fire and unload infantry, MANPADS, and mortars so the frontline actually moves.\r\n\r\nThe flight model sits between arcade and simulation: enough weight to respect momentum, enough forgiveness to survive learning it.\r\n\r\nThen the Collection launcher asks whether you want Heliborne or Enhanced Edition.\r\n\r\nChoose the original.\r\n\r\nThe maps repeat, the presentation has aged, and public multiplayer now has more helicopters than pilots. But solo and co-op still preserve something almost no other game offers.\r\n\r\nThe rockets clear the hill.\r\n\r\nThe troops make it yours.",
